{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_a64d1a605f2246cd967f5161","type":"tool_result","content":"## `__init__` summary (with short quoted snippets)\n\nRather than reproducing the whole method, here's its structure with the key lines quoted exactly:\n\n- **Signature:** takes `cells` (a `Mapping[T, list[CellAgent]] | Iterable[T]`) and an optional `random: Random | None`.\n- **Cell storage:** if `cells` is a dict it's stored directly; otherwise the method builds one via `\"self._cells = {cell: cell.agents for cell in cells}\"`.\n- **Capacity assignment (the line you asked about):**\n\n  ```python\n  self._capacity: int = next(iter(self._cells.keys())).capacity\n  ```\n\n  Note there is **no empty-collection guard** here — if `_cells` is empty, `next(iter(...))` raises `StopIteration` at construction time.\n- **Random setup:** if no generator is passed, it creates one with a `\"random = Random()  # FIXME\"` note (unseeded).\n\n## Capacity property\n\nThere is **no capacity property** anywhere in this file. `_capacity` is only a private attribute, set once in `__init__` and never read or exposed within the code shown.\n\n## Empty-collection guards in the random selectors\n\nNeither method guards against an empty collection:\n\n- `select_random_cell` is just `\"return self.random.choice(self.cells)\"`.\n- `select_random_agent` is just `\"return self.random.choice(list(self.agents))\"`.\n\nBoth would raise an `IndexError` from `random.choice` if called on an empty collection.\n\n**Minor observation:** `select()` constructs `CellCollection(cell_generator(...))` without forwarding `self.random`, so filtered collections get a fresh unseeded generator."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65204899-2904-4d8a-948d-b64eb6e184e1","uuid":"33a5c767-899f-41e6-bc10-3f28b4cde904","timestamp":"2026-09-03T19:07:17.078Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":3426,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"## `__init__` summary (with short quoted snippets)\n\nRather 