{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788462632-CJRLGRFzzWRSx3fniZl9","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Empty `CellCollection`s now work without errors.\n\n**The bug** — `mesa/experimental/cell_space/cell_collection.py:52` unconditionally grabbed the capacity of the first cell via `next(iter(self._cells.keys())).capacity`. With no cells, `next()` on an empty iterator raised `StopIteration`. This hit both direct construction (`CellCollection([])`) and any `.select()` filter that matched nothing, since `select()` builds a new collection from the filtered generator.\n\n**The fix** — a conditional guard, so `_capacity` is typed `int | None`: taken from the first cell when the collection is non-empty, `None` when it's empty. No flags or extra steps — the constructor detects emptiness itself, and since every space type (`OrthogonalMooreGrid`, `Network`, `VoronoiGrid`, etc.) funnels collection creation through this one `__init__`, they're all covered.\n\n**Behavior for non-empty collections is untouched** — the capacity is still read from the first cell exactly as before, and all existing methods (`__iter__`, `__len__`, `cells`, `agents`, `select`, `select_random_cell`, `select_random_agent`) behave identically.\n\n**Verified:**\n- `CellCollection([])` constructs fine: `len == 0`, `_capacity is None`, empty `cells`/`agents`, and `select()` on it returns an empty collection\n- A 10-cell collection filtered with `lambda cell: False` yields an empty collection with `_capacity is None`, including with `at_most=5`\n- Non-empty collections still report their capacity (`2` in my check) and random selection still works\n- `tests/test_cell_space.py`: **22 passed**, including the new `test_empty_cell_collection` regression test I added covering both initialization and filtering paths\n\nOne thing worth knowing: the upstream project fixed this identically in PR #2502 (\"cell_space: Allow CellCollection to be empty\"), so this change keeps you in line with where mesa went. Also note `select_random_cell()` / `select_random_agent()` on an *empty* collection will still raise `IndexError` from `random.choice` — that's pre-existing upstream behavior and there's no meaningful value to return, but I can make those return `None` instead if you'd like.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65204899-2904-4d8a-948d-b64eb6e184e1","uuid":"4b3d3f6e-ee11-4d7d-a6b5-700454593e3d","timestamp":"2026-09-03T19:10:47.439Z","request_id":"gen-1788462632-CJRLGRFzzWRSx3fniZl9"}
